      "body": "Verified on Linux \u2014 the half the body says was not run, plus a note on the host delegation.\n\n- `cmake --build build --target libs` \u2192 clean.\n- **Module-level differential**: `readelf -sW build/core/libs/libs/unpatched/libSceLibcInternal.prx` lists `atoll_nid_postfix` as a `GLOBAL FUNC` with the change; rebuilding the same way with this file at `main` gives **0**. So the export is real and it lands in the module.\n- **The delegation is safe here, unlike its sibling.** `long long atoll(const char*)` returns `long long`, which is 64 bits on Windows too, so handing the conversion to the host C runtime gives the guest the width it expects. That is worth one sentence in the body: `atol` next door needed an explicit `strtoll` precisely because the host's `long` is 32 bits on Windows (#1868), and a reader who sees this one delegating to the host will ask why that one could not.\n\n**For the merge bar**: #1578 line 32 lists `atoll` among the missing `libSceLibcInternal` imports, so the \"why\" exists \u2014 quoting the title's unresolved-import line here would put it alongside the fix.\n\nNot verified: Windows; the runtime half \u2014 the export is proven present, not proven called.\n\nWritten with AI assistance.\n",
